From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LIVI appliance
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 00:30:00 +1030
Subject: [PATCH] unisocwifi: set the AP channel before starting the AP

hostapd only writes the DS Parameter Set element (which carries the
channel) into beacons for 2.4 GHz (hostapd_eid_ds_params() returns early
for hw_mode=a), and the firmware apparently takes the AP channel from that
element: with hw_mode=a hostapd reports the interface AP-ENABLED while
nothing is ever radiated, on any 5 GHz channel. 2.4 GHz works, 5 GHz
receive works, so it is only the AP transmit path that never learns which
channel to use.

Set the channel explicitly with WIFI_CMD_SET_CHANNEL right before
WIFI_CMD_START_AP, the way the IBSS join path already does. A failure is
logged and does not abort the AP start.
---
 unisocwifi/cfg80211.c | 18 ++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+)

--- a/unisocwifi/cfg80211.c
+++ b/unisocwifi/cfg80211.c
@@ -1086,6 +1086,24 @@
 			(settings->hidden_ssid != 0 ? settings->ssid_len : 0),
 		       tail, tail_len);
 
+	/* The firmware picks the AP channel up from the beacon's DS Parameter
+	 * Set element, which hostapd emits for 2.4 GHz but not for 5 GHz
+	 * (hostapd_eid_ds_params() only writes it for g/b modes). Without it
+	 * the AP reports ENABLED and never radiates on 5 GHz. Set the channel
+	 * explicitly first, the way the IBSS path already does.
+	 */
+	if (settings->chandef.chan) {
+		int cret;
+		u8 channel = ieee80211_frequency_to_channel(
+				settings->chandef.chan->center_freq);
+
+		cret = sprdwl_set_channel(vif->priv, vif->ctx_id, channel);
+		if (cret)
+			wl_ndev_log(L_ERR, ndev,
+				    "%s set channel %u failed(%d)\n",
+				    __func__, channel, cret);
+	}
+
 	ret = sprdwl_start_ap(vif->priv, vif->ctx_id, (unsigned char *)mgmt,
 			      mgmt_len);
 	kfree(mgmt);
